        "paragraph_id": "15DE1938",
        "text": "The resulting GLM-momentum equations are given by:"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 20111,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 567,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 499,
        "paragraph_id": "0577F0A1",
        "text": "where τsx and τsy are the wind shear stresses, τbx and τby are the bed shear stresses, η is the water level, Fx and Fy are the wave-induced stresses, Fv,x, and Fv,y are the stresses induced by vegetation, νh is the horizontal viscosity and f is the Coriolis coefficient. Note that the shear stress terms are calculated with the Eulerian velocities as experienced by the bed and not with the GLM velocities, as can be seen in (2.45)."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
